`Dieu 122 — loss prevention and limitation: definition; the policyholder and insured person act on their own initiative, notify the insured event at once and follow the insurer's guidance (the notice is tested by Dieu 46 and 21(2)(dd)); the insurer trains, funds and builds works or hires monitors; the authorities publicise (duties and measures without a testable fact beyond the assertion of compliance; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Duties and measures."

